"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Also don't forget cases where there is only one maximal side for edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are no more than 3·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" edges. So iterating over every parallelepiped with structure "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"map"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to store maximums works in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/a002eaf6956aba1d0e43f039349eebb93a309b582a36326d14afef858108330e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 3."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Kniaz"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kniaz"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"733E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/733/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"733E - Sleep in Class"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Olga is always able to go beyond stairs. To prove that let's consider some segment of stairs. If we enter it from upper step then we move down until reaching 'U' which reverses our moving direction. After that we leave segment from above. Now this 'U' became 'D' and other symbols remained the same as they were either visited twice or not visited at all. So we enter segment once again from upper step, this time we proceed to next 'U'. And at the some point we leave segment from below. It will happen in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 turn where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — number of 'U' symbols in segment. Leaving segment from above when it's entered from below is done in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 turns, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - number of 'D' symbols in segment. It can be proven the same way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we can divide stairs into three parts: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Segment below current step "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Current step "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Segment above current step "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be easily seen that we will go beyond stairs either from 1"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"st"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" or from 3"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"rd"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" segment. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let's calculate values of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for every step. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — number of 'U' symbols in prefix of stairs "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (exluding "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — number of 'D' symbols in suffix (exluding "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" =  = '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"')"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" =  = '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"')"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We will also need values of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - time in seconds to leave stairs from below as if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is always equal to 'D' and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - time in seconds to leave stairs from above as if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is always equal to 'U'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's obvious that by moving iterator by one position to the right we increase distance to every calculated symbol 'U' by 1, so it's  + 2 for each symbol to overall time (we go to this symbol and back to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If previous symbol was 'U' then we should add 2 more to overall time. In total this will be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·2. And as we moved one step away from exit we should increase time by 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·2 + 1"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And it's the same for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·2 + 1"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And finally let's derive formula to get answer in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1) for each step."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Olga will go beyond stairs from the side which has least amount of obstacles. If amounts are equal then it's the matter of current letter. Let's imply that we are exiting from both sides at the same time and just subtract from time the part from the side opposite to exiting one. So we should subtract "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (it depends on exiting side), where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is position in string of last visited element of side opposite to exiting one. And also subtract doubled distance between current step and last visited obstacle multiplied by number of unvisited onstacles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So if we go beyond stairs from below then this is the derived formula:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"posd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"posd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") - 2·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"posd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"posd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — reversed array of indices (positions in string) of 'D' symbol."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"kd"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ku"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — number (not position) of last visited element from above. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is 0 if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 'D', 1 if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 'U'. (This will be reversed on exiting from above)"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Answer for last step is calculated the same way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For deriving formula for exiting from above you will also need "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"posu"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — array of indices (positions in string) of 'U' symbol (not reversed this time)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Автор задачи: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Kniaz"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kniaz"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"733F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/733/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"733F - Drivers Dissatisfaction"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you choose any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 roads then price of reducing overall dissatisfaction is equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"min"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", .."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"с"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is price of reducing by 1 dissatisfaction of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th edge. So the best solution is to choose one edge and reduce dissatisfaction of it until running out of budget."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's construct minimal spanning tree using Prim or Kruskal algorithm using edges of weights equal to dissatisfaction and calculate minimal price of reducing dissatisfaction. Time complexity — "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/9da868919fa4eafb00ba5b3937648442c6f9570abcfa73635c5ab43b31ff76fd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we can iterate over edges implying that current is the one to be reduced to minimum. For example, for every edge we can build new MST and recalculate answer. It's "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/57bccc3b677660021b30a1d0fc9fe78a081c8921c8ce58d50976fdd2e2dd0d27.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Therefore we should use this fact: it's poinless to reduce dissatisfaction of edges which weren't selected to be main."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we can transform original MST instead of constructing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" new ones. Add next edge to MST, now it contains a cycle from which edge with maximal dissatisfaction is about to be deleted. This can be achieved in such a way: find LCA of vertices of new edge in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" and using binary lifting with precalc in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f9edda04d142988747c93c4e7ffb9141d5687b7dd90520c29948f28573b3d1a1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" find the edge to delete."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity — "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/6753ea5ac4c950d5da5313c4d2355e2c8be8dfccad870138a1162bbaccf4f292.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Автор задачи: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I want to thank Mikhail Piklyaev ("},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/awoo"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"awoo"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":") for translation of tutorial!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/48133"}